# What `gcloud builds submit` may upload. This is a separate exposure from
# .dockerignore and has to be kept beside it: the whole directory is tarred and
# put in a staging bucket before any Dockerfile is read, so a path excluded from
# every image is still uploaded unless it is excluded here as well. With no
# .gcloudignore at all gcloud synthesises one from .gitignore, and everything
# tracked in git - the dugout included - goes up.
#
# The first two lines are correctness rather than housekeeping. `COPY arena/ ./`
# runs after `uv sync` has built /app/.venv, and `COPY game/frontend/ ./` runs
# after `npm ci` has built node_modules. If the context carried either, this
# Mac's aarch64 virtual environment and host-built native modules would land on
# top of the container's and the image would fail somewhere strange and late.
**/.venv
**/node_modules
# A stale local pitch build would be copied in and then overwritten by the build
# stage, which works until the day it does not.
**/dist
# The suites have no business in an image that faces the internet.
**/tests
**/__pycache__
**/.pytest_cache
**/*.db
**/.env
# History, and it is large. The tag deploy.sh builds under is worked out on this
# machine, so nothing in the build needs a repository.
.git
docs
# The dugout embeds the Antigravity CLI and runs shell commands unrestricted,
# and it has no business in an image that faces the internet - nor in a bucket
# reachable by everyone with build access to the project.
dugout
